update public.curriculum_units as c set description = v.description from (values
('07218bee-f13c-40af-a0b4-5a65bfc6d3a7'::uuid, 'Plants continue to grow in particular regions because they contain meristematic tissues. This section examines where plant growth occurs, how cell division and cell expansion contribute to it, and how environmental conditions influence the growth of roots and shoots.'),
('15c07a23-8dec-4f91-956b-d9323df77535'::uuid, 'Growth depends on more than the organism''s inherited characteristics. The supply of nutrients, hormones, health and environmental conditions can all influence how an organism grows and develops. This section examines these factors and considers how they may limit or support normal growth.'),
('289a410f-ee53-4440-b2f8-f6c44d5866f5'::uuid, 'Plant growth takes place mainly in meristematic regions where cells divide and later become specialised. In this lesson, you will identify the main growth regions in roots and shoots and explain how cell division, elongation and differentiation contribute to plant growth.'),
('3fc751ef-2a01-47e7-8a7b-02e99bfc16e6'::uuid, 'The general patterns of growth can now be considered in a plant, where growth is concentrated in regions containing meristems. This theme focuses on the growth regions of roots and shoots and the processes that increase their length and form new tissues.'),
('511c927a-8c79-4682-b120-ab1b491c0e4f'::uuid, 'The growth patterns seen in plants and humans are shaped by conditions within the organism and in its surroundings. This theme brings together genetic, nutritional, hormonal and environmental influences, showing why growth rates and final size can differ.'),
('7db5b080-4f70-4799-8fac-806c0294c462'::uuid, 'Growth involves a lasting increase in size or dry mass, while development includes the changes that occur as an organism becomes more mature. In this lesson, you will distinguish growth from development, identify ways of measuring growth and interpret a typical growth curve.'),
('7e7acd33-5f9d-4fc2-b8b4-2e409e70062f'::uuid, 'Human growth and development continue through a series of recognisable life stages. In this lesson, you will describe the main stages from infancy to old age and explain the physical and developmental changes associated with childhood, adolescence and adulthood.'),
('84039e4a-5f2d-4274-adf3-589b00f84db0'::uuid, 'Growth is influenced by inherited information and by the conditions in which an organism lives. In this lesson, you will explain how genes, nutrition, hormones, health and environmental factors affect growth, and give examples of how unsuitable conditions can interfere with normal development.'),
('866427fc-d4ec-458c-bb0e-aa274fc0756f'::uuid, 'Plant growth is concentrated in specialised regions, whereas human growth involves coordinated changes across the body. This theme introduces the stages of human growth and development and the characteristic changes that occur during each stage of life.'),
('88e7ba9a-9b71-4660-9815-c53ca7af7b52'::uuid, 'Human growth involves changes in body size and proportions, while development includes physical, mental and reproductive maturation. This section follows the main stages of human development and examines the changes that occur from infancy through childhood, adolescence and adulthood.'),
('8f209e89-41d9-4f78-92c5-1da3d643cd55'::uuid, 'Growth is a measurable change in an organism, but the pattern is not always the same throughout its life. This section examines how growth can be represented and compared, including changes in size, mass and body proportions. You will learn to interpret growth patterns and distinguish growth from the wider process of development.'),
('f0e5430f-e02e-413b-b899-0d83be7f8a07'::uuid, 'The meaning of growth becomes clearer when changes are followed over time. This theme introduces ways of measuring growth and interpreting growth curves, showing how the rate of growth may change during an organism''s life.')
) as v(id,description) where c.id=v.id and c.description is distinct from v.description;
